{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-07T14:02:47Z","content":"The runner **`th2-ansid-run1`** does not permanently store credentials for target servers on its local disk. Instead, credentials flow through a secure, just-in-time delivery mechanism orchestrated by Semaphore:\n\n---\n\n### 1. In Semaphore: The Inventory & Access Key Mapping\n\nEvery task running on `th2-ansid-run1` is linked to an inventory defined in Semaphore UI:\n* **Inventory ID `2` (`Dev`)**:\n  * Targets: `inventories/dev/hosts.yml`\n  * Runner Tag: `dev` (which routes tasks directly to `th2-ansid-run1`)\n  * **SSH Key ID**: Linked to Access Key ID **`4`** named **`spui-runner-ssh-dev`** (type: SSH Private Key).\n\n---\n\n### 2. End-to-End Delivery: How the Runner Receives the Credentials\n\n```text\n+----------------------------+\n|      Semaphore Server      |\n|  (Project Infra Mgmt ID 1) |\n+--------------+-------------+\n               |\n               | 1. Job payload encrypted with runner's RSA public key\n               |    (contains: git commit, inventory, and decrypted SSH private key)\n               v\n+----------------------------------------------------+\n|  Runner: th2-ansid-run1 (Docker container)         |\n|  - Decrypts job with /var/lib/semaphore/runner.key |\n|  - Writes ephemeral SSH key in memory/temp file     |\n|  - Injects into Ansible execution environment      |\n+----------------------+-----------------------------+\n                       |\n                       | 2. SSH connection on port 30\n                       |    as user 'spui-runner'\n                       v\n+----------------------------------------------------+\n|  Target Server (e.g., trp-wextd-be1:30)            |\n|  - User: spui-runner                               |\n|  - Auth: /etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner       |\n|  - Sudo: /etc/sudoers.d/spui-runner (NOPASSWD)     |\n+----------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n1. **Job Dispatch & Encryption**:\n   * The runner maintains an outbound API connection to `https://semaphore.corp.intranet.local/api` using its runner token (`SEMAPHORE_RUNNER_TOKEN`).\n   * When a job is trigger\n<truncated 255 bytes>\nr decrypts the job payload in memory using its durable private key ([`config/runner.key`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/docs/semaphore-runner-install.md#L64)).\n   * The SSH private key is temporarily made available to Ansible (via `--private-key` or an internal SSH agent) strictly for the lifespan of that specific task.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Target Server Configuration: The `spui-runner` Identity\n\nOn the target servers (`trp-*d-*`), the corresponding identity has been provisioned by the Ansible role [`roles/bootstrap_spui_runner`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/roles/bootstrap_spui_runner/tasks/main.yml):\n\n* **SSH Port**: Hardened port **`30`** (specified under `ansible_port: 30` in [`inventories/dev/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/dev/hosts.yml#L5)).\n* **User**: **`spui-runner`**, member of group `SSH_Users` (authorized in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config`).\n* **Authorized Key**: Placed in `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner`:\n  ```text\n  ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIFXxaA6I6XHKt1N9KMolZQQ7abBDA3r+RDl3iFc3l/Jo semaphore-runner\n  ```\n  *(Configured via `spui_runner_pubkey` in [`inventories/dev/group_vars/all.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/dev/group_vars/all.yml#L7)).*\n* **Privilege Escalation**: Drop-in file `/etc/sudoers.d/spui-runner` granting <span style=\"color:green\">`spui-runner ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL`</span>.\n\n---\n\n### 4. What About Fresh Servers? (The Bootstrap Inventory)\n\nWhen a brand-new target server does not yet have the `spui-runner` account:\n* Semaphore has a dedicated inventory: **Inventory ID `4` (`Dev Bootstrap (superuser)`)**.\n* This inventory uses Access Key ID **`5`** (`superuser-trp-wextd-dbm1`, username/password) to connect initially as `superuser` on port 30 and run [`playbooks/bootstrap-spui-runner.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/playbooks/bootstrap-spui-runner.yml).\n* Once bootstrapped, all standard day-to-day playbooks switch back to Inventory ID `2` using key-based authentication as `spui-runner`.","thinking":"**Tracing Login Information Retrieval**\n\nThe process begins within the Semaphore UI where an inventory, identified by a specific ID (e.g., `2`), is defined. This inventory, linked to a hosts file (e.g., `inventories/dev/hosts.yml`) and a runner tag (e.g., `\"dev\"`), includes an assigned access key. This access key, with a specific ID (e.g., `4`), is designated for SSH access (named `spui-runner-ssh`).\n\n\n**Deconstructing Job Execution Details**\n\nThe provided SSH access key is utilized with a login username during job execution. Sudo privileges are handled either through a specified key ID or pre-configured passwordless sudo on the target host, and will be incorporated if required. The job dispatch involves encryption of the payload, then decryption by the runner container using its durable private key.\n\nOnce the job is queued, the encrypted payload containing the SSH key is sent from the server to the runner. The decrypted SSH key is then either written to a temporary file, or fed directly to Ansible via parameters for execution. The defined inventory specifies connection details including the target's IP address.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
